# Slice 346 (the author 2026-11-10, LMX_blog/2026-11-10.md#receiver-args-only and #composed-form-breaks-structure): a
# receiver in the tail of a form declares inside it and never turns the outer name into a variable. The author's line
# `timeout: ms: int: time 500` declares the Structure timeout with the Structure ms inside and the place time in it --
# read and written through the path timeout\ms\time. `holder: int: time` is a Structure holder with the field time.
# `i: int: 5` and `x: 4` declare Structures with a value inside (one field each), no variable of an int.
timeout: ms: int: time 500
int: seen timeout\ms\time
timeout\ms\time := 7
int: again timeout\ms\time
holder: int: time
i: int: 5
x: 4
int: n_i length(i)
int: n_x length(x)
